{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-85242-r4523250","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Herb Bubble Bread","sourcePageId":85242,"sourceRevision":"4523250","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-13T17:18:19Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Herb%20Bubble%20Bread&oldid=4523250","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:20.515Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for bread","Category:Recipes using bread flour","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using milk","Category:Recipes using parmesan","Category:Recipes using savory","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"3493306058845a05cd945e6062afd9111a98c3239c5b127eac64d209c6bfd48a","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| category = Bread recipes\n| Yield = 12–16 rolls/buns<br>OR 6–8 mini loaves<br> OR 1 regular-sized loaf\n| time = Prep: 8 to 10 minutes.<br/>Cooking: 15 minutes+ depending on size\n| difficulty = 3\n}}\n__NOTOC__\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Herb bubble bread''' is nice type of bread that is a good accompaniment to any meal. This recipe is for use with a bread machine.\n==Ingredients==\n===Dough===\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* 4 ounces [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 standard [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]], beaten \n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] softened [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n* 1 tablespoon white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 2 ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] bread [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 2 ¼ teaspoons active dry [[Cookbook:Yeast|yeast]]\n\n===Herb mixture===\n* ¼ cup butter or margarine\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* ¼ cup grated [[Cookbook:Parmesan Cheese|Parmesan cheese]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|garlic powder]]\n* ½ teaspoon dried minced [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* ⅛ teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Savory|savory]]\n\n== Special equipment ==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Bread Machine|Bread machine]]\n* [[Cookbook:Loaf Pan|Loaf pan]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Measure all ingredients for the dough into the bread pan. Set your bread machine to the dough setting.\n#Remove [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]] after it's finished mixing in the bread machine.\n#In a small bowl, combine the herb mixture in the order listed.\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 350°F (180°C).  \n#Divide the dough into 12–16 equal parts and shape into balls.\n#Roll each ball into the herb mixture and arrange in greased loaf pan.\n#Cover with a cloth and let rise in a draft-free place until doubled (about 30 minutes).\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 25–30 minutes or until brown.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n*All ingredients should be at room temperature (70–80°F/21–27°C).\n*Cooking times may vary between various models of ovens.\n*This dough can also be made into 12–16 rolls/buns, 6–8 mini loaves, or 1 regular sized loaf of bread.\n*To cut the cooking time in half, preheat oven to 400°C. Then bake for 15 minutes and your rolls/buns or mini loaves will come out golden brown. You might want to cook it slightly longer for a regular size loaf of this bread.\n*You can use [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|all-purpose flour]] if you don't happen to have bread flour.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for bread]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using parmesan]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using savory]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Herb Bubble Bread","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 ounces water","sourceText":"4 ounces water","amountText":"4 ounces water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"4 ounces milk","sourceText":"4 ounces milk","amountText":"4 ounces milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 teaspoon salt","sourceText":"1 teaspoon salt","amountText":"1 teaspoon salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 standard egg, beaten","sourceText":"1 standard egg, beaten","amountText":"1 standard egg, beaten","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 tablespoons softened butter or margarine","sourceText":"2 tablespoons softened butter or margarine","amountText":"2 tablespoons softened butter or margarine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tablespoon white granulated sugar","sourceText":"1 tablespoon white granulated sugar","amountText":"1 tablespoon white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 ½ cups bread flour","sourceText":"2 ½ cups bread flour","amountText":"2 ½ cups bread flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id